<title>JAPAN: Citicorp launches 5.4% yen/dlr samurai.</title>
<headline>Citicorp launches 5.4% yen/dlr samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/dollar</p>
<p>dual-currency samurai issue was announced by lead manager Daiwa</p>
<p>Securities on Thursday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Citicorp</p>
<p> AMT		 25 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    5.4 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  18 April 2000</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  18 April 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	April 7 to April 17</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P A+, Moody's A1</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Daiwa Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi</p>
<p>NOTE: The exchange rate was fixed at $4,091.66 to 500,000 yen.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
